    <div class="prose text-themed">

      <h3>Self-Tuning Eval Protocol</h3>
      <p>The eval-tune-store loop was executed as follows on the 52-document legal vault:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Agent:</strong> Claude Opus 4.6 via Claude Code with the HEBBS skill file.</li>
        <li><strong>LLM backend for indexing:</strong> OpenAI GPT-4o-mini (proposition extraction, contradiction detection).</li>
        <li><strong>Embedding model:</strong> EmbeddingGemma-300M (768 dimensions, local ONNX inference).</li>
        <li><strong>Eval queries:</strong> 20 queries generated by the agent after reading <code>hebbs list --format json</code>. Distribution: 10 similarity, 3 temporal, 2 causal, 3 analogical, 2 contradiction.</li>
        <li><strong>Expected keywords:</strong> 85 total keywords across 20 queries, manually verified against vault contents.</li>
        <li><strong>Baseline run:</strong> All queries with <code>--strategy similarity -k 5</code>. Result: 50/85 keywords (59%).</li>
        <li><strong>Tuned run:</strong> Per-query strategy, weights, k, and cue refinement selected by agent. Result: 75/85 keywords (88%).</li>
        <li><strong>Stored strategies:</strong> 5 high-importance memories encoding generalized retrieval rules.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        The four remaining gaps (4/20 queries with missing keywords) involved specific dollar amounts and proper nouns buried in dense contract language that the embedding model did not surface in the top-k results regardless of strategy. These represent a floor set by embedding quality rather than retrieval configuration.
      </p>

